Sofia / Marcus,

I have reviewed the current draft and source materials. The story can
publish IF the following three boxes are ticked by the fact-checker:

1. The COI link (Hartmann equity stake in Helios Civil Works GmbH + board
   seat in Riverbend Foundation) is corroborated by at least two independent
   sources (corporate registry + annual report is sufficient).

2. The on-record admission from Hartmann is captured in the audio recording
   (the automated transcript is not sufficient for legal purposes -- it
   contains known transcription errors per the file header).

3. The vote minutes, if obtained, confirm whether the abstention was
   formally recorded. If the minutes show she voted and did not abstain,
   that is a major new fact and the story becomes stronger.

Please ensure the fact-checker documents all three in output/.

-- Legal

